{"kind":"report","text":"Complete preliminary static reassessment: R3 revision 7 at 524ba4539237b23ce6f85928510cc062ceadfefd and R2 revision 10 at e2b22c244c2b8a7e801a54f89a06b8d9943a53f6. Live tracking: own request 32733cff and promise b56a8360 under governing direction d4e07064. This is an assessment of unfiled design drafts, not a guarded verdict, implementation approval or adoption. Retired commissioning records and prior reports are immutable reading evidence only.\n\nCoverage and identity. The root independently verified each exact head and its direct parent, da20beebeccf7950a31e78f876c57de4ba912421 for R3 and dc0fdd74f7b56441e1b940470982504a6003cf75 for R2. Both parents were fully read. The root now read every byte of both complete unified-8 diffs, including corrections: R3 108,919 bytes / 108,903 characters / 992 lines; R2 32,315 bytes / characters / 306 lines. Only main and corrections changed in each; the facts files are byte-identical. Whole decisive source/attribution/ancestry/root guards were cross-read. Three independent static readers checked complete changed sections and whole clock/replay, staging/pin and cancellation contracts against R1v6 667c3318. Current six-file identities are below. This transfers the earlier whole-file read only over verified unchanged bytes; it does not claim new runtime evidence.\n\nOne P2, high confidence: excluding the start from F admits an exact foreign staged commit without its attribution. R3 main 1722–1724 says the candidate is never in F and visits only its parents. Let U be an unpublished commit staged under unrelated commitment K2 in L2, with sole parent D, the destination head. V holds a valid current hold under K, fetches exact U into that fork, stages U as an own live root, and proposes U with no selected report or earlier manifest. The snapshot includes L2's live staged ref for U. The walk visits D, stops at the branch, and produces F=[]; 1771 passes. Authors at 1683–1689 come from K, its inputs and superseded versions, omitting K2's contributors. Those contributors can then qualify as independent reviewers.\n\nThis is a visible foreign Git ID, not copied content, an omitted/late ref, retired roots or published history. No declared creation proof blocks it: 1649 checks performer/hold/holder/instance; 1662–1664 authenticates source identifiers; 1953 requires fork possession; 2002–2004 checks ref value, canonical fork provenance and object closure. 2172–2174 permits staging an existing closure when the caller holds their own valid hold. 'Who made' at 1646 supplies no enforceable original-production test, and Git author text is explicitly excluded at 1927. Thus the witness violates the stated guarantee at 1938–1940 that no commit staged for other work is carried in by ID without a fact naming it.\n\nRepair must distinguish the candidate's own current root from foreign refs targeting the candidate. Preserve the rule that the candidate cannot certify itself or stop parent traversal; inspect the start for unrelated staged provenance, requiring the appropriate input/selection or earlier-manifest attribution. Resolve matching multiple roots without letting the new own ref mask the foreign one. Retain that judgment in the historical snapshot/record and replay. Include exact-U direct reuse alongside the repaired D/U/I parent case, plus legitimate own staging/reuse and previously attributed same-ID reuse. Do not derive authors from Git text or reject all ordinary newly staged candidates.\n\nPrior repairs hold in the proposal. Historical ancestry replay retains canonical snapshot bytes, digest/count, head, stops, prior checks and carried F; replay derives against retained inputs, never current refs, and answers incomplete when required evidence is missing. Own-root stops require earlier admitted evidence; the current root cannot stop its parent walk, and all prior F is carried. No separate circular-certification defect was established. Snapshot completeness and preservation remain explicitly trusted: staged-ref-read, vouched for by the staging runtime on H2.\n\nObservationUse distinguishes run/read identity and fresh versus reused observations. Equal-value fresh reads at one clock reading are valid; reuse requires consistent prior history and a later clock reading. A replay checks that record's consistency while explicitly trusting performed reads, fresh-value provenance and restart claims; it cannot prove an unrecorded restart or a real-time bound. Backward-clock rules now follow R1's due-first ordering: due transitions stop all entries; otherwise time-free outcomes may be clamped. The separate non-entry read/stream/fence answers stay closed. W6/W7 name H5 plus H6.\n\nR2v10/R3v7 cancellation now uses the actual refusal reason. A never-reserved out-of-date publication answers ended/not-reserved/out-of-date, not reserved. Final-update-first stays final and free; result-first records the answer and stays frozen until the final update. Pending/lost withdrawal answers do not freeze already-final merge items. Results remain effect-free and do not reopen final items. R1 verifies result-send provenance under its stated source-runtime trust; independent replay derives the handler result. No new cancellation defect was established.\n\nTwo nonblocking wording corrections: R3 247–249 calls all observation-bearing entries 'acts', although reservation entries also judge freshness; say that such entries judge freshness and are never clamped. At 1856–1858, 'first four' leaves the fifth selected-report guard's refusal unclassified; name its refusal explicitly. No reachable changed-selection witness was established.\n\nArchitecture: retained immutable inputs, admitted prior-check stops and explicit trust make the earlier replay claims coherent; fix the start classification before relying on the attribution guarantee. Security: the exact-ID bypass affects author exclusion and counted review independence, even with every grant/hold/ref guard satisfied. Simplification: keep one preparation order and one replay contract; narrow start exclusion rather than adding an unproved authorship oracle.\n\nScope and open duties remain intact. R1 O1–O10 and R2 forms/adoption are still owed; ancestry-stale and the full pin ancestry record are proposed dependencies, not silently implemented declarations. Bounds 4096 walked commits, 64 F and 64 stops remain proposals for R4 to measure. Snapshot size is explicitly unbounded U18 and owned, not an undisclosed bound. H1/H2/H4/H5/H6 remain assumptions. Unknown export/mint/create/push/delete outcomes, pins, cleanup, restart/retirement custody, all browser/agent paths, real-host, cold/manual and cost evidence remain owed. Estimates impose no scope cut. Static reads only: no repository/package execution, tests, private diagnostics, provider effects, source edits, merges or deployment.\n\nSix-file identity ledger (path relative to notes):\nR3 main 2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md: 236690 bytes, 2897 lines, SHA256 4a012bc4f98863f58b4658755e4bd405807ff97be3d4d1a6725cdabffac51d07, blob fa4666d9e2e8278403e0a9e1719f79885d11a75c.\nR3 corrections: 39405 bytes, 229 lines, SHA256 fb66a4fe6be246a9d5e8411cd22a7d0fa3312b9af643391233c8dd7735bb8ccf, blob d27eca16d1723413a4b21268dd68df6a5d571e82.\nR3 publication-and-authority-facts: 84111 bytes, 723 lines, SHA256 12db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0, blob ab371b65ffd5bc07e015f5172661fd9e9a559193.\nR2 main 2026-10-04-lane-forms-and-browser-flow.md: 212055 bytes, 2621 lines, SHA256 030a716fce01a47a8f35a1a8430c145a8e1cfc35925fff86065080933a26508f, blob a4f93968eb85478d6b2f4a5cb742ead1d207d1df.\nR2 corrections: 45522 bytes, 369 lines, SHA256 16fcd91b6450526119dc20f508e8ea2847405fdbf5f7777f3f3ac7a01515f520, blob 14edcd545e0773f7af8d68a4e97faafe804cd0e2.\nR2 github-documentation-2026-10-04: 77287 bytes, 559 lines, SHA256 7b7d1b49f50dd61c5ae40c976273ab1e920a837e60cb72c7cef7284f7f2fde94, blob 7b87d0970c7db157ce31fd4166d8f246f863